:28Z","updated_at":"2026-09-04T21:48:38Z","due_on":"2025-09-15T00:00:00Z","closed_at":"2025-09-18T17:13:14Z"},"comments":1,"created_at":"2025-03-08T16:32:45Z","updated_at":"2025-03-16T11:10:09Z","closed_at":"2025-03-12T15:38:10Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/103822","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103822","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103822.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103822.patch","merged_at":"2025-03-12T15:38:10Z"},"body":"Fixes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102847\r\n\r\nAs you can see in the images below, the ports for child nodes with size flag (expand + any of the shrink flags) were drawn as if the node fills all its available space. \r\nAlso, the positions used for connections did not account for the expanded space.\r\nThis pr makes both consistent, by placing the port where the child nodes are(at half of their height).\r\n\r\nBefore:\r\n![graphnode_ports_position_wrong](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4c16cbd9-d4aa-476b-93b1-9ccc9ee50bbf)\r\n(I added flat styleboxes for the slots so the issue is more clear)\r\n\r\nThis pr:\r\n![graphnode_ports_position_fixed](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a2541e48-39ed-43e9-9b63-6af49ac2b655)\r\n\r\nChanges:\r\n- Changed slot_y_cache calculations in  _resort function so ports will be drawn correctly for expanded children.\r\n- Similarly calculate the port_cache.pos in _port_pos_update function so the connection matches the port's position.\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repit